\section*{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitations}

\paragraph{Model scale.}
Experiments are validated at ${\leq}6.9$B parameters across six decoder-only transformer families.
Whether the temporal lead shortens or vanishes at frontier scale (7B+) is open; encoder-decoder and non-autoregressive architectures are untested.

\paragraph{Data domain and scale.}
Training data is drawn from a 5K-document WikiText-103 subset, three orders of magnitude smaller than typical pre-training corpora.
C4 generalization experiments introduce a pre-training data confound: Pythia was pre-trained on the Pile, which includes C4-overlapping data, so observed differences from the WikiText baseline may partly reflect domain familiarity.

\paragraph{Short time series.}
With $T{=}10$ (11 data points), threshold onset detection is power-limited (0/8 in most conditions under $3\sigma$ calibration) and Toda--Yamamoto achieves only moderate detection (3--4/8 at $\alpha{\geq}0.50$).
Our method recommendation (PermG) is robust at $T{=}10$; both supplementary methods could improve at $T{\geq}20$.

\paragraph{Regime boundary and intervention scope.}
The onset boundary ($\alpha_c{\approx}0.476$) and canary blind spot ($\alpha{=}0.10$) rest on limited seeds; finer $\alpha$ resolution and multi-seed confirmation are needed.
Intervention experiments validate predictive cessation only at $\alpha{=}1.0$ across two model scales; efficacy under partial contamination or accumulate-mode training~\cite{dey2024breaking} is untested.

\paragraph{Scope.}
Canary claims are scoped to distinct-$n$ diversity metrics~\cite{li2016diversity}, not model collapse broadly~\cite{schaeffer2025position}, as the perplexity channel proved spurious after differencing.
Replace-only protocol; accumulate-mode may exhibit qualitatively different canary dynamics.

